# =============================================================================
#  PetPal — Android UI strings  ·  English (en)  ·  SOURCE LOCALE
# =============================================================================
#  This file lists every player-facing text string in the Android app so it can
#  be translated. To make a translation, copy this file to
#  "Android_strings_<code>.lang" (e.g. Android_strings_DE.lang) and translate the
#  values. Keys are kept parallel to 3DS_strings_EN.lang where the two apps share
#  a concept (SPECIES.*, MOOD.*, ITEM.* …) so translations can be reused.
#
#  HOW TO TRANSLATE — please read:
#   • Translate ONLY the text to the RIGHT of the first '=' on each line.
#   • Do NOT change the KEY on the left of '=' — it identifies the string and is
#     the SAME in every language. The KEY (AREA.NAME) tells you where the text
#     appears; the "# src:" note per section tells you which file it comes from.
#   • Keep every {placeholder} EXACTLY as written — the app swaps in a name or
#     number at runtime. You MAY move a {placeholder} to fit your grammar, but
#     keep all of them and don't translate the word inside the braces. Each is
#     explained in a "# ph:" note above the line.
#   • Emojis are part of the copy — keep them; move if needed.
#   • Keep punctuation like the arrow → and the ✓ mark. Keep \n as a line break.
#   • Lines starting with '#' are notes for translators and are ignored by tools.
#
#  Note: source/res/values/strings.xml currently holds only APP.NAME and
#  QR.PRIVACY_NOTICE; every other string below is inline in Kotlin/Compose.
#  Preview-only sample text in model/SampleData.kt (fake friends, demo award
#  copy) is NOT listed here — players never see it.
# =============================================================================


